.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/@alloc/quick-lru Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "quick-lru [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/quick-lru.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/quick-lru) [![Coverage Status](https://coveralls.io/repos/github/sindresorhus/quick-lru/badge.svg?branch=master)](https://coveralls.io/github/sindresorhus/quick-lru?branch=master)"
.PP
.RS 4
Simple \fR“Least Recently Used” (LRU) cache\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Useful when you need to cache something and limit memory usage\&.

.PP
Inspired by the \fR\fRhashlru\fP algorithm\fP, but instead uses \fR\fRMap\fP\fP to support keys of any type, not just strings, and values can be \fRundefined\fP\&.
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install quick\-lru
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
const QuickLRU = require('quick\-lru');

const lru = new QuickLRU({maxSize: 1000});

lru\&.set('🦄', '🌈');

lru\&.has('🦄');
//=> true

lru\&.get('🦄');
//=> '🌈'
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "new QuickLRU(options?)"
Returns a new instance\&.
.SS "options"
Type: \fRobject\fP
.SS "maxSize"
\fIRequired\fP\\ Type: \fRnumber\fP

.PP
The maximum number of items before evicting the least recently used items\&.
.SS "maxAge"
Type: \fRnumber\fP\\ Default: \fRInfinity\fP

.PP
The maximum number of milliseconds an item should remain in cache\&. By default maxAge will be Infinity, which means that items will never expire\&.

.PP
Lazy expiration happens upon the next \fRwrite\fP or \fRread\fP call\&.

.PP
Individual expiration of an item can be specified by the \fRset(key, value, options)\fP method\&.
.SS "onEviction"
\fIOptional\fP\\ Type: \fR(key, value) => void\fP

.PP
Called right before an item is evicted from the cache\&.

.PP
Useful for side effects or for items like object URLs that need explicit cleanup (\fRrevokeObjectURL\fP)\&.
.SS "Instance"
The instance is \fR\fRiterable\fP\fP so you can use it directly in a \fR\fRfor…of\fP\fP loop\&.

.PP
Both \fRkey\fP and \fRvalue\fP can be of any type\&.
.SS "\&.set(key, value, options?)"
Set an item\&. Returns the instance\&.

.PP
Individual expiration of an item can be specified with the \fRmaxAge\fP option\&. If not specified, the global \fRmaxAge\fP value will be used in case it is specified on the constructor, otherwise the item will never expire\&.
.SS "\&.get(key)"
Get an item\&.
.SS "\&.has(key)"
Check if an item exists\&.
.SS "\&.peek(key)"
Get an item without marking it as recently used\&.
.SS "\&.delete(key)"
Delete an item\&.

.PP
Returns \fRtrue\fP if the item is removed or \fRfalse\fP if the item doesn't exist\&.
.SS "\&.clear()"
Delete all items\&.
.SS "\&.resize(maxSize)"
Update the \fRmaxSize\fP, discarding items as necessary\&. Insertion order is mostly preserved, though this is not a strong guarantee\&.

.PP
Useful for on-the-fly tuning of cache sizes in live systems\&.
.SS "\&.keys()"
Iterable for all the keys\&.
.SS "\&.values()"
Iterable for all the values\&.
.SS "\&.entriesAscending()"
Iterable for all entries, starting with the oldest (ascending in recency)\&.
.SS "\&.entriesDescending()"
Iterable for all entries, starting with the newest (descending in recency)\&.
.SS "\&.size"
The stored item count\&.

.PP
